Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: gliff
Source: https://github.com/omacom/gliff
Comment:
 The source package carries two trees: the program (the tag tarball) and vendor/
 (the crates from Cargo.lock, shipped as the component "vendor" so the build needs
 no network). The Files paragraphs for vendor/ are generated by
 scripts/vendor-copyright.py from each crate's Cargo.toml license field; each
 crate's copyright holders are the authors named in that crate's Cargo.toml and
 the license files inside the crate's directory. The crate libdbus-sys carries the
 C source of libdbus 1.14.4 in vendor/libdbus-sys/vendor/dbus/, which the build
 does not compile (gliff links Ubuntu's libdbus-1-3); the Files paragraphs for
 that directory are written by hand from Debian's dbus 1.14.10-1~deb12u1
 copyright file, for the files the crate carries. The release's NOTICE says the
 binaries link OpenH264 (BSD-2-Clause, Cisco Systems).

